WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.301
What to carry forward.

2
00:00:01.581 --> 00:00:08.557
Start with exact search and do the arithmetic; for many internal tools it’s fast enough and its recall is perfect.

3
00:00:08.837 --> 00:00:20.229
When you need an ANN index, HNSW is the usual default if memory allows; IVF with product quantization is the tool for collections too big for RAM.

4
00:00:20.509 --> 00:00:27.208
Every index has a dial that trades recall for speed, and adding one changes your results, not just your latency.

5
00:00:27.488 --> 00:00:36.341
So measure recall@k against exact search on real queries, pick a setting against a stated target, and keep measuring as the data grows.

6
00:00:36.621 --> 00:00:43.832
Week 2 takes you from raw documents to the chunks you’ll index; the vector store choices there build directly on this lesson.
